{"base_rate":0.3530183727034121,"brier":0.13173556430446193,"bss":0.4232152363573298,"bss_hi":0.5102267038204259,"bss_lo":0.3379446422491333,"chart":{"base":[367.2,129.1],"fp":[347.1,278.7],"lead":"62,274.9 272,250.4 482,197.9 692,111.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.42 — higher than 80% of cities","fp":"low end +8pp, high end +8pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 86% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 12%; promised 96% → rained 86%"},"rel":"80.6,415.6 409.6,234.5 668.6,92.5"},"country":"PL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07518372703412074,"ess":432.8246667851428,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Szczecin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Szczecin rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>90%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGRAMBOW-SCHWENNENZ, 12.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.42, ranked 43 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(18&ndash;84) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>380</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>90%</b></td><td class='num'>102</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Szczecin</b> <span class=\"muted\">Poland</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;35% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 35% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.42</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>18&ndash;84\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Szczecin &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Szczecin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.226473684210525,376.2526315789474 110.52594594594595,298.3783783783784 198.87384615384616,199.88333333333398 309.95359999999994,90.80000000000001 377.8022641509435,31.564150943397124 409.7788235294118,18.0 409.7788235294118,28.70588235294116 377.8022641509435,86.67924528301887 309.95359999999994,158.74666666666667 198.87384615384616,274.66666666666663 110.52594594594595,357.4054054054054 60.226473684210525,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"253.501312335958\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"253.501312335958\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.226473684210525,349.4315789473684 110.52594594594595,288.5405405405405 198.87384615384616,242.0 309.95359999999994,129.62666666666667 377.8022641509435,93.54716981132071 409.7788235294118,53.68627450980392\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 380 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.226473684210525\" cy=\"349.4315789473684\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"110.52594594594595\" cy=\"288.5405405405405\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 40%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"198.87384615384616\" cy=\"242.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"309.95359999999994\" cy=\"129.62666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 53 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.8022641509435\" cy=\"93.54716981132071\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 102 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.7788235294118\" cy=\"53.68627450980392\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(35%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Szczecin the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.52) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.29).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.290</td><td class='num'>13.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.302</td><td class='num'>7.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.479</td><td class='num'>7.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.517</td><td class='num'>5.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.42894,"lon":14.55302,"n":762,"n_cities":216,"name":"Szczecin","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006289473684210527,"n":380,"obs":0.08947368421052632,"sig":true},{"hi":0.28,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.1483783783783784,"n":74,"obs":0.25675675675675674,"sig":true},{"hi":0.55,"lo":0.28,"mean":0.39794871794871794,"n":78,"obs":0.38461538461538464,"sig":false},{"hi":0.85,"lo":0.55,"mean":0.7117333333333332,"n":75,"obs":0.6933333333333334,"sig":false},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.85,"mean":0.9033962264150945,"n":53,"obs":0.7924528301886793,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9937254901960786,"n":102,"obs":0.9019607843137255,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":12.8,"provisional":false,"rank":43,"rank_hi":84.0,"rank_lo":18.0,"reliability":0.006626208625811354,"resolution":0.10080544262585378,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"szczecin","station":"GRAMBOW-SCHWENNENZ","timezone":"Europe/Warsaw"}